@startuml
title Historical insecure notes flow represented in the 2025 evidence

actor "User" as User
participant "Web client" as Web
participant "API gateway" as Gateway
participant "Authentication service" as Auth
participant "Notes service" as Notes
database "Database" as DB

note over User,DB
This diagram is a faithful modernization of the security-relevant behavior
described by the original sample_notes_app.uml. It is diagram evidence,
not proof that a deployed implementation had these weaknesses.
end note

== Unauthenticated listing ==
User -> Web : Open notes page
Web -> Gateway : GET /api/notes without credentials
Gateway -> Notes : Forward request
Notes -> DB : Query notes without owner scope shown
DB --> Notes : All notes
Notes --> Web : Notes response

== Login and repeated failures ==
loop Repeated attempts
  User -> Web : Submit username and password
  Web -> Gateway : POST /api/login
  Gateway -> Auth : Validate credentials
  Auth --> Web : Invalid credentials
end
note right of Auth
No failed-attempt limit or temporary lockout is shown.
MFA is also absent from the historical diagram.
end note

== Create and export ==
User -> Web : Submit note title and body
Web -> Gateway : POST /api/notes/create
Gateway -> Notes : Create note
note right of Notes
Input validation and audit recording are not shown.
end note
Notes -> DB : Insert note
User -> Web : Request export
Web -> Gateway : GET /api/notes/export
Gateway -> Notes : Export request
Notes -> DB : Query all notes
DB --> User : Exported data
note right of Gateway
Rate limiting and owner-scoped export are not shown.
end note

== Detailed error ==
DB --> Notes : Database error with sensitive field detail
Notes --> Web : Detailed error response
Web --> User : Display internal error

== Delete ==
User -> Web : Delete note
Web -> Gateway : DELETE /api/notes/{id}
note right of Gateway
Owner-scoped authorization is not shown.
The UI flow has no confirmation step.
end note
@enduml

